course: dictionary
lesson: 5464
title: A French word in English
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Lapin» is a French word, so a French sentence can give you its meaning. In «J'ai un lapin», the rest of the sentence shows that lapin means rabbit.
explain: In English, lapin is rare. You will mostly meet it for rabbit fur used in clothes, which is sometimes dyed to look like more expensive fur, or on old-style menus where it means rabbit meat. For the animal itself, English speakers say rabbit.
explain: Listen for the nasal ending: lapin sounds like «la-PAN», a bit like "an" said through the nose. Other French words with the same sound are le pain (bread), le vin (wine) and la main (hand).
fact: «Lapin» is the French word for rabbit.
fact: «J'ai un lapin» means "I have a rabbit" in French.
fact: In English, lapin can mean rabbit fur used for clothes, often dyed to look like more expensive fur.
fact: On old-style menus, lapin can mean rabbit meat.
fact: In English, say «rabbit» for the animal.
exercise: «J'ai un lapin.» What does lapin mean? | Bird | Fish | *Rabbit | Fox
exercise: In English, what is lapin mostly used for? | A kind of bread | A type of car | *Rabbit fur for clothes, sometimes dyed | A French school subject
exercise: Which French word means bread? | *le pain | le lapin | la main | le vin
test: Which French word means wine? | le pain | la main | le lapin | *le vin
test: An old menu lists lapin. What might it mean? | A hat | A cup of tea | A sheep's coat | *Rabbit meat
exam: Why should you say «rabbit» in English instead of lapin? | *Lapin is rare in English and mostly about fur or old menus, so rabbit is the everyday word | Rabbit is only a French word | Lapin is a rude word | Lapin means a bird
